(A name declared in EVERY branch of an if/otherwise chain is definite -
 whichever branch runs, it has been declared by the time the chain ends,
 so the read after it is in order and must still compile. Bug #79's fix
 makes the top-level walk fill its scope in declaration order instead of
 from the whole-program set, and this is the shape that would break if
 the branch merge were not doing its own half of the job.)

a number called mode is 1.

If mode is 1 then,
  a text called verdict is "first".
Otherwise,
  a text called verdict is "second".

Print verdict.
